  "answer": "On 25 GitHub issues from load-bearing dependency trackers that this estate already cites on disk (7 anthropics/claude-code from RES-0115, 18 modelcontextprotocol/inspector from the RES-0043 captured README), estate blockage labels are all false: RISK-REGISTER.md is absent and no receipt records any of these URLs as a work-stopper. A citation is not a blockage label, and labels were not read from issue title/body. The preregistered field score (threshold>=4) false-predicted blockage on 4/17 train issues and 1/8 holdout issues. Blocker-class precision/recall are undefined on a zero-positive set, so 'which fields predict that an open issue will actually block us' is NOT VALIDATED as a blocker detector. Holdout metrics are reported separately; an in-sample-only figure is NOT VALIDATED. Vendor-acked inspector bugs with milestone+bug often score as predicted-blockers, which on this estate's labels are false positives: those fields track vendor acknowledgement, not this estate's impact. SUCCESS:RES-0142. SUCCESS:RES-0142 emitted only when the artifact at output_path exists, is non-empty, parses against output_schema, the 25 estate-labelled issues are scored from frozen observable tracker fields, holdout metrics on 8 issues are reported separately from the 17-issue train split, the near-identical 30-source control fires EARLY, the diverse 30-source control stays silent, and five historical citation documents replay from on-disk sources. In-sample-only figures are labelled NOT VALIDATED. Any other terminal state is FAILED:RES-0142 <classification> with the diagnostic tail.",
